# Rendered Kubernetes manifests, produced by `make k8s_render` / scripts/k8s-preflight.sh
# --render. These are COPIES of infrastructure/k8s-manifests with the application image
# resolved to a concrete digest, and they must never be committed: the committed manifests
# deliberately carry an unresolvable placeholder so that an apply cannot silently run a
# build other than the one intended. A digest checked in here would defeat that.
/rendered/

# Scratch files written by `make alerts_configmap`: the alert rule file as the Kubernetes
# ConfigMap projects it, plus a unit-test file pointed at that projection. Both are removed
# on exit and are dot-prefixed so the rule_files glob (alerts/*.yml, non-recursive) cannot
# see them even mid-run; they are listed here so an interrupted run cannot leave one staged.
/alerts/tests/.configmap-projection.yml
/alerts/tests/.configmap-projection_test.yml
